.TH GENETREE 1 2000-1月 "perturb_combined" "perturb_combined"
.SH NAME
perturb_combined \- Run a combined in silico intervention on a set of genes at the same time.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIperturb_combined(\fBtree\fR as <generic> XGBoostGRN, 
\fBgenes\fR as any, 
\fBmode\fR as <integer> InterventionMode = [Knockout], 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Run a combined in silico intervention on a set of genes at the same time.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBtree\fB \fR\- the trained [XGBoostGRN](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.GeneTree.XGBoostGRN) model object.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBgenes\fB \fR\- a character vector of the gene id that are perturbed together.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmode\fB \fR\- 
 the intervention mode of all of the target genes: \fBKnockout\fR, \fBKnockdown\fR,
 \fBOverexpression\fR or \fBCustom\fR.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment object.. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
one [InterventionResult](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.BioSystem.Intervention.InterventionResult) object of the combined intervention, the
 non additive synergy/antagonism effect of the gene combination is kept;
 an R# error message object is returned when the prediction fails.
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
the \fBSpec\fR property of the result object is a synthetic intervention
 specification whose gene name is the \fB+\fR joined id list.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
geneTree
.SH FILES
.PP
